===== path d
Develop: goldens, record/replay and other tools for working on toolpath itself (built only with the `develop` feature)

Usage: path d [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  baseline  Capture, check and diff the baseline: every recording's snapshots, stage by stage
  webmock   The record/replay server: `run <agent> record|replay …` or `serve` (its own options: `path d webmock -- --help`)
  agents    The agent CLIs tests and replay run: fetched only as agents.lock names them, hash-verified, cached by hash, never on PATH
  model     Regenerate the goldens object model, docs/model/model.json (its own options: `path d model -- --help`)
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
===== path d agents
The agent CLIs tests and replay run: fetched only as agents.lock names them, hash-verified, cached by hash, never on PATH

Usage: path d agents [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list   List what the lock names and whether each entry is cached
  fetch  Download one agent's blob from the url in the lock, verify its sha256, keep it in the cache
  path   Print the cache path of an already fetched agent (fails if it is not cached and valid)
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --lock <LOCK>
          The lock file
          
          [default: agents.lock]

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
===== path d agents fetch
Download one agent's blob from the url in the lock, verify its sha256, keep it in the cache

Usage: path d agents fetch [OPTIONS] <AGENT>

Arguments:
  <AGENT>
          

Options:
      --lock <LOCK>
          The lock file
          
          [default: agents.lock]

      --target <TARGET>
          Rust-style target (default: this machine)

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
