===== path d baseline
Capture, check and diff the baseline: every recording's snapshots, stage by stage

Usage: path d baseline [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list            List the golden sets in the manifest
  roundtrip       Round trips IR -> adapter -> IR for every set and adapter: key paths lost and gained, text and tool-use survival (check pins today's losses and gains; a new one of either fails)
  shed            What information is shed when a transcript becomes a Toolpath document and is projected out: per stage events and bytes in/out, key paths lost, renames, dropped fields with one example
  init            Capture the standard sets from the repo's own fixtures
  capture         Capture a golden set from a fixture, hermetically, to every target; with --all re-capture every set in the manifest
  check           Check the whole baseline: runs the tests that are the check (`cargo test -p toolpath-goldens`, then `cargo test -p path-cli --features develop --test goldens`), so this and `cargo test` cannot disagree; exit 1 on any failure. With a set name or a flag below, re-runs the manifest goldens in-process only (the same `Goldens::check` the path-cli test calls)
  diff            Show how a fresh run differs from a set's goldens
  capture-live    Capture one REAL headless session of an installed agent hermetically (credentials copied or forwarded into a temp HOME only), leak-check it, then capture it as a golden set
  capture-claude  Alias for `capture-live claude`
  provenance      Print the provenance of an installed agent binary: code signature and upstream match (needs network for the upstream check; no credentials)
  help            Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --root <ROOT>
          Repository root holding `goldens/` (default: nearest ancestor of the cwd that has one)

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
===== path d baseline capture
Capture a golden set from a fixture, hermetically, to every target; with --all re-capture every set in the manifest

Usage: path d baseline capture [OPTIONS] [HARNESS] [FIXTURE]

Arguments:
  [HARNESS]
          Source harness
          
          [possible values: codex, claude, copilot, pi]

  [FIXTURE]
          Fixture file (a session log in the harness's own format)

Options:
      --name <NAME>
          Name of the golden set (default: the harness name)

      --root <ROOT>
          Repository root holding `goldens/` (default: nearest ancestor of the cwd that has one)

      --project <PROJECT>
          Project directory to place the session under (claude, pi; default: the fixture's cwd)

      --all
          Re-capture every set already in the manifest

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
===== path d baseline capture-claude
Alias for `capture-live claude`

Usage: path d baseline capture-claude [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --bin <BIN>
          Path to the agent executable (default: $<AGENT>_BIN, then PATH, then ~/.local/bin/<agent>)

      --root <ROOT>
          Repository root holding `goldens/` (default: nearest ancestor of the cwd that has one)

      --name <NAME>
          Golden set name (default: <agent>-session)

      --model <MODEL>
          Model to run (claude defaults to claude-haiku-4-5-20251001; others use their own default)

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
===== path d baseline capture-live
Capture one REAL headless session of an installed agent hermetically (credentials copied or forwarded into a temp HOME only), leak-check it, then capture it as a golden set

Usage: path d baseline capture-live [OPTIONS] <HARNESS>

Arguments:
  <HARNESS>
          Possible values:
          - claude
          - codex
          - pi
          - copilot
          - cursor:   Not supported: cursor-agent keeps its transcript in a protobuf store the adapter does not parse
          - opencode: Not supported: opencode keeps its transcript in SQLite; a golden input must be a single file

Options:
      --bin <BIN>
          Path to the agent executable (default: $<AGENT>_BIN, then PATH, then ~/.local/bin/<agent>)

      --root <ROOT>
          Repository root holding `goldens/` (default: nearest ancestor of the cwd that has one)

      --name <NAME>
          Golden set name (default: <agent>-session)

      --model <MODEL>
          Model to run (claude defaults to claude-haiku-4-5-20251001; others use their own default)

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
===== path d baseline check
Check the whole baseline: runs the tests that are the check (`cargo test -p toolpath-goldens`, then `cargo test -p path-cli --features develop --test goldens`), so this and `cargo test` cannot disagree; exit 1 on any failure. With a set name or a flag below, re-runs the manifest goldens in-process only (the same `Goldens::check` the path-cli test calls)

Usage: path d baseline check [OPTIONS] [NAME]

Arguments:
  [NAME]
          Check only this set, in-process (default: the whole baseline through `cargo test`)

Options:
      --allow-producer-drift
          Report a moved producer (the running `path` binary, or repo code differing from the pin) as a warning row instead of a problem

      --root <ROOT>
          Repository root holding `goldens/` (default: nearest ancestor of the cwd that has one)

      --no-qualifier
          Skip `qualifier review` on purpose. Without this flag a missing `qualifier` binary ($TOOLPATH_GOLDENS_QUALIFIER, else `qualifier` on PATH) is a failure, not a skip

      --in-process
          Run the manifest goldens in-process instead of through `cargo test`

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
